  info: 'The order Araneae, commonly known as spiders, are eight-legged Arthropods
    that can extrude silk through their spinnerets to construct webs. Spiders are
    found in every continent excluding Antarctica, and live in nearly every land
    habitat. Araneae are not considered insects, despite many believing so.


    Source: 
    https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider '
